Rule 1 (inputs must be broadcastable along all dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : (shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∨ shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = 1)
>>
Rule 2 (avoid zero-vs-non-singleton mismatches)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : if shape(v_1, i) = 0 then (shape(v_2, i) = 0 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = 1) else if shape(v_2, i) = 0 then (shape(v_1, i) = 0 ∨ shape(v_1, i) = 1)
>>
Rule 3 (out must be a Tensor, not a scalar)
{v_3 : tensor} |= ndim(v_3) ≥ 0
